---
title: "Copy Button"
description: "Copies the text of another element to the clipboard and announces the result."
tags: [utility, accessibility, javascript]
usage: |
  Give a button `data-copy-target` with the id of the element to copy, and put a
  status element right after the button. Then call `initCopyButtons()`:

  ```js
  import { initCopyButtons } from "./copy-button.js";

  initCopyButtons(); // or initCopyButtons(root, "[data-copy-target]")
  ```

  The status reads "Copied!" or "Copy failed" for two seconds. Copying needs a
  secure context (HTTPS or localhost).
accessibility: |
  - The status element needs `role="status"` (or `aria-live="polite"`) so the
    result is announced.
  - Give the button a label that says what is copied when there are several on a
    page, for example "Copy install command".
customProperties:
  "--copy-button-cursor": "Cursor over the button."
  "--copy-status-gap": "Space between the button and the status text."
  "--copy-status-font-size": "Font size of the status text."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<pre><code id="copy-source">deno task serve</code></pre>
<button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="copy-source">Copy</button>
<span class="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>

<script type="module">
  import { initCopyButtons } from "./copy-button.js";

  initCopyButtons();
</script>
